mastrm -- Master Mind=====================    mastrmThe computer hides a code of four coloured pegs, drawn from white, black,red, green, yellow and blue, and you have ten guesses to break it.  Typea guess as four colour names; it is scored with a `b' for every peg of theright colour in the right place and a `w' for every peg of the rightcolour in the wrong place.  Read the b's and w's across your guesses todeduce the code.You can also make the code for the computer to guess, and turn on coaching.Peter E. Granger, released to the public domain via Usenet, 1987.  MasterMind is a trademark of Invicta Plastics; this game is not licensed by orconnected with them.  Originals in SRC/mastrm/ORIG.